import{_ as o,o as t,c as d,a2 as r}from"./chunks/framework.BUOFcz_J.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"An outside Agent opens a folder with Rho and works in it","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"records/outside-agent-episode.md","filePath":"records/outside-agent-episode.md"}'),a={name:"records/outside-agent-episode.md"};function s(n,e,h,i,c,l){return t(),d("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[r('<div class="warning custom-block"><p class="custom-block-title">Historical record</p><p>This page records what happened on a date, with its observed failures and limits. It is not a requirement for the current implementation. Current behaviour is in <a href="/Rho/docs/reference/status">Status</a>.</p></div><h1 id="an-outside-agent-opens-a-folder-with-rho-and-works-in-it" tabindex="-1">An outside Agent opens a folder with Rho and works in it <a class="header-anchor" href="#an-outside-agent-opens-a-folder-with-rho-and-works-in-it" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;An outside Agent opens a folder with Rho and works in it&quot;">​</a></h1><p>Updated 2026-11-10. The user asked an Agent in WorkBuddy (5.9.3) to &quot;使用rho 启动该项目&quot; in their own airway project, <code>~/Projects/气道平滑肌-地塞米松</code>, then to make a new workspace with an illustrated analysis, then &quot;Draw the volcano plot in the notebook; I will select the genes I care about.&quot; The user found it slow, and asked for more guidance for people (that Rho is a page in the browser) and for Agents (to start Rho quickly), with the user&#39;s scenario simulated to find what hurts. This episode reads that session, runs the same requests with parallel trials, changes Rho, and runs them again.</p><h2 id="the-workbuddy-session" tabindex="-1">The WorkBuddy session <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-workbuddy-session" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The WorkBuddy session&quot;">​</a></h2><p>From WorkBuddy&#39;s own session file for that conversation. The Rho Skill in <code>~/.workbuddy/skills/rho</code> was imported seven minutes after the conversation began, so the conversation did not list it (<a href="/Rho/docs/records/workbuddy-connector-episode">WorkBuddy connector</a>).</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Request</th><th>Wall time</th><th>What the time went to</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Start the project</td><td>203 s</td><td>16 shell and file calls before starting: <code>rho --help</code>, <code>rho connect --help</code>, <code>ls -laR .rho</code>, the project&#39;s <code>.workbuddy</code> memory, old state folders, and a grep of the installed <code>cli.js</code>. It found an earlier state, <code>~/.rho-state</code>, with <code>~/Projects</code> as root, and started Rho in the foreground as a WorkBuddy background task with that root, so every folder in <code>~/Projects</code> became a candidate project. It opened the page with <code>rho --pair --root</code>, a five-minute one-time link</td></tr><tr><td>New workspace, illustrated analysis</td><td>about 21 min</td><td>A sub-agent read Rho&#39;s source for 5 min 19 s to learn what a workspace is. The Agent then called Rho&#39;s HTTP API with the state&#39;s operator credential from scripts in <code>/tmp</code>, guessed a resource kind and retried. It concluded that &quot;Rho 的文档视图是源码编辑器，没有渲染预览&quot; and made a separate HTML report: it had placed the report in <code>rho.editor</code>, the source editor it found in the code, while Rho has a Markdown reader (<code>markdown.reader</code>)</td></tr><tr><td>Volcano plot to select genes</td><td>about 19 min</td><td>A sub-agent read Rho&#39;s source for 12 min 29 s to find how a figure becomes selectable. The cells then ran through the HTTP API as the operator, not as an Agent session</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The Agent called no Rho tool in that session. WorkBuddy&#39;s MCP configuration held three Rho servers its own Agent had added, <code>rho-project</code> for this project among them, but WorkBuddy runs such a server only after the person approves it, and none was approved (<a href="/Rho/docs/records/workbuddy-connector-episode">WorkBuddy connector</a>). Nothing told the Agent another way in than the operator&#39;s HTTP API.</p><h2 id="trials" tabindex="-1">Trials <a class="header-anchor" href="#trials" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Trials&quot;">​</a></h2><p><code>scripts/outside-agent-trials.mjs</code> gives a fresh Claude Code (<code>claude -p</code>, model <code>westlakehpc/glm-5.3-flash</code>, Claude Code 2.1.319 to 2.1.321) a copy of the airway project in a throwaway home, <code>rho</code> on PATH from this checkout&#39;s build, and its shell and file tools with nothing to approve; <code>open</code> is replaced by a recorder. Variant <code>bare</code> has only <code>rho</code>; <code>skill</code> also has the Rho Skill this checkout ships in <code>~/.claude/skills/rho</code>. Runs go in parallel. The volcano case first runs <code>rho open --no-browser</code>, as if the person had asked earlier, so it starts with Rho running and the project open, and without Rho&#39;s tools in the session, as in WorkBuddy.</p><p><strong>Baseline</strong> (main after the setup-report batch: <code>--background</code> and <code>--status</code>, no <code>rho open</code>). The runs sat inside this checkout, whose instructions and source one Agent read, and the first Node on PATH was 22.17.0, which sent two <code>skill</code> runs looking for another Node; later runs fixed both. Still, the open question showed:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Run</th><th>Seconds</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>bare-3, skill-2</td><td>33, 43</td><td>Rho started with <code>--background</code> on the folder&#39;s parent; the folder not opened as a project</td></tr><tr><td>bare-1</td><td>241</td><td>Three minutes of <code>rho connect</code>, <code>--pair</code> and <code>--grant</code> until a grant registered the folder</td></tr><tr><td>bare-2</td><td>261</td><td>Copied the project to a shorter path after a managed run hit the 103-byte socket limit</td></tr><tr><td>skill-1, skill-3</td><td>179, 185</td><td>Stopped on the Node check (one asked the person to install Node), Rho not started</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Three of six opened a browser (the Skill&#39;s start example had no <code>--open</code>); two of six made the folder a project.</p><h2 id="what-was-changed" tabindex="-1">What was changed <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-was-changed" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;What was changed&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong><code>rho open [FOLDER]</code>.</strong> Uses the running Rho that has the folder, else the one for <code>--state-dir</code> (<code>~/Rho/state</code>), starting it in the background with <code>~/Rho/projects</code> as its projects folder when nothing runs there. It opens the folder as a project where it is, opens <code>&lt;url&gt;/#project=&lt;id&gt;</code> in the default browser and prints what to tell the person: that Rho is a workspace in their web browser, what is on the page, that no account or code is needed, and how to stop it, then how an Agent works there. A folder outside the projects folder is opened by <code>project.open</code> with its full path, which only the state&#39;s operator credential may name; it becomes a project of the person&#39;s own tab, as a folder chosen in the system dialog, and stays theirs after a restart. Earlier Rho versions refuse the full path, and <code>rho open</code> says what to do then.</li><li><strong><code>rho tool index|resolve|call|read|list --as NAME</code>.</strong> Rho&#39;s four Agent tools from a shell. It grants the project to session NAME as <code>rho connect</code> does, starts <code>rho --mcp</code> on that grant for one call and prints the tool&#39;s reply, so the work is the Agent&#39;s session&#39;s, as over MCP.</li><li><strong><code>rho --help</code></strong> opens with what Rho is and <code>rho open</code>, <code>--status</code> and <code>--stop</code>, then the Agent commands; plugin development moved under &quot;Less common&quot;. Every Agent observed, WorkBuddy&#39;s included, read the help first.</li><li><strong><code>.rho/README.md</code>.</strong> Rho writes it when it holds a project. It says the files there are internal and names <code>rho open</code>, <code>rho tool</code> and <code>rho connect</code>.</li><li><strong>The Skill</strong> starts with <code>rho open</code> when the person asks to start or open Rho, without the install checks, then what to tell the person, then <code>rho tool</code> when the tools are not loaded, Notebook cells rather than separate scripts, and the page&#39;s address in each report. The setup page&#39;s closing report leads with the browser page and names <code>rho open</code>. A <code>--background</code> start prints a line saying Rho is a workspace in the browser.</li></ul><h2 id="after-the-change" tabindex="-1">After the change <a class="header-anchor" href="#after-the-change" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;After the change&quot;">​</a></h2><p><strong>Open the folder</strong> (&quot;使用rho 启动该项目&quot;), 3 <code>bare</code> and 3 <code>skill</code> runs:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th></th><th>Seconds</th><th>Calls</th><th>Folder a project</th><th>Browser opened</th><th>Person told it is a browser page</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>bare</td><td>33, 16, 25</td><td>10, 2, 5</td><td>3 of 3</td><td>3 of 3</td><td>3 of 3</td></tr><tr><td>skill</td><td>16, 17, 18</td><td>3 each: the Skill, <code>rho --version</code>, <code>rho open</code></td><td>3 of 3</td><td>3 of 3</td><td>3 of 3</td></tr></tbody></table><p>By hand on this Mac, <code>rho open</code> with nothing running returned in 0.87 s, and the address showed the project, with its earlier work, in Chrome. After <code>rho --stop</code> and a plain start, the person&#39;s tab still listed the folder.</p><p><strong>Draw the volcano plot</strong> with Rho open and no Rho tools loaded. Every run drew it as a cell in the Notebook through <code>rho tool</code>; each figure record has a point layer of 17,157 to 17,165 marks, one per gene with an adjusted p-value, bound mark by mark:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Round</th><th>Seconds</th><th>First Rho command at</th><th>Reads of Rho&#39;s state files</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>rho tool</code> and help, before <code>.rho/README.md</code></td><td>121, 238, 229, 408</td><td>40–183 s</td><td>1–36</td></tr><tr><td>with <code>.rho/README.md</code></td><td>203, 192, 124, 258</td><td>18–78 s</td><td>0–1</td></tr><tr><td>with the report line in the note and the Skill</td><td>264, 88, 99, 177</td><td>13–47 s</td><td>0–4</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Every run in the first round began by listing <code>.rho/</code> and reading its state files, as WorkBuddy did (<code>ls -laR .rho</code>); one read them for two minutes, and one walked its own figure record through <code>rho tool read</code> for two more. In the second round each read the note and went to <code>rho tool</code>. None of its four answers gave the page&#39;s address: they said to select points &quot;in the Notebook&quot;, which a person who does not know Rho is a browser page cannot place. No <code>skill</code> run of this case loaded the Skill, as the request does not name Rho: the note in <code>.rho/</code> is the guidance an Agent meets there. With a line asking for the page&#39;s address in each report, two of the third round&#39;s four answers gave it (<code>http://127.0.0.1:…/#project=…</code>), one pointed to &quot;本页右侧的 Notebook 面板&quot; without it, and one did not say where.</p><h2 id="ci" tabindex="-1">CI <a class="header-anchor" href="#ci" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;CI&quot;">​</a></h2><p><a href="https://github.com/YuLab-SMU/Rho/actions/runs/42736131288" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">CI 42736131288</a> on <code>553b7f78</code>: the first attempt failed only in Test win32-x64, where <code>agent-observation.test.mjs</code> (&quot;browser observes only its project…&quot;) got <code>host_unavailable</code> with <code>os error 2</code> on the project Host&#39;s named pipe. The rerun passed every job, and the installed check ran <code>rho open</code> on a folder outside the projects folder and <code>rho tool index</code> through <code>rho</code>/<code>rho.cmd</code> on the four platforms, in about 1.8 to 2.7 s. The failure is Core&#39;s: on Windows <code>IpcListener::bind</code> creates no pipe, the accept thread that <code>serve</code> starts after printing its ready line makes the first instance, and each next one only on its next loop, so a client right after ready, or between two connections, can find none (read in Rho-core <code>8bed8ef</code>). It is open work for Rho-core.</p><h2 id="not-done" tabindex="-1">Not done <a class="header-anchor" href="#not-done" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Not done&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>WorkBuddy&#39;s desktop app and model (Hy4) were not run again. The trials here use Claude Code; the <a href="/Rho/docs/records/workbuddy-connector-episode">WorkBuddy connector</a> episode runs WorkBuddy&#39;s own agent core with another model.</li><li>The workspace request (workspace, rendered report, figures in views) was not repeated. Whether <code>rho tool</code> leads an Agent to <code>markdown.reader</code> is unobserved.</li><li><code>rho open</code> and <code>rho tool</code> were run on macOS only; Windows (<code>rho.cmd</code>) runs in CI.</li><li>No person has used the opened page from these trials; the trials count what the Agent said.</li><li>Half the volcano answers still do not give the page&#39;s address. The note and the Skill only ask for it; nothing in a Notebook cell&#39;s reply names the page.</li></ul>',25)])])}const w=o(a,[["render",s]]);export{u as __pageData,w as default};
